WEB SOURCE SHAPE (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ArchivedPage.tsx is a thin wrapper: `usePageTitle('Archived notifications')` + a `<PageContainer
title subtitle copyLink actions={<Link to="/notifications/inbox"><ArrowLeft/> Back to inbox</Link>}>`
whose only child is `<InboxBody archived={true} vehicles={vehicles} rules={rules} />`. The page binds
two data sources at its level — `useVehicles()` (GET /vehicles) + `useAlertRules()` (GET /alerts/rules)
— and passes their results straight into the shared inbox body. The manifest record
(apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:notifications/Archived) extracts exactly the page-level
surface: dataSources [useAlertRules, useVehicles], NO named panels, NO charts, NO maps, states
[success], and the three i18n strings notifications.archived.{title,subtitle,backToInbox}
(requiredCount=4 = 1 state + 3 strings). The actual list/bulk-action body is the *separately-shipped*
parity unit feature-views/InboxBody (P4 artifact 0183, already DONE — its 19 Apple files live in
apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/InboxBody.*). Faithful, non-narrowing parity (covenant #2/#5) =
reproduce the PageContainer chrome (title + subtitle + copyLink + the Back-to-inbox action) AND host
the real InboxBody view fixed to the archived tab (DRY — no re-implementation), driven by the page
model's InboxBodyModel(archived: true). In the Apple InboxBody contract the rule/vehicle context is
delivered through the InboxSource snapshot (InboxUpdate.rules / .vehicles), so `useVehicles`/
`useAlertRules` reach the inbox there and are re-surfaced on the page model (model.vehicles /
model.rules) under the same web call-site names.

