OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Notifications/**`. That path
does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app targets list `Sources` +
`TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` plus
`TeslaSync/Features` — but the compiled canonical *page* home is `Sources/Features/<Domain>/**`). The
repo's real, compiled page home — where the sibling P7 notifications pages (AuditLog, Webhooks) ship
and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups) — is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Notifications/**`. The page therefore ships there, the faithful
equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Notifications`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the SAME reconciliation the
sibling notifications-Webhooks + notifications-AuditLog P7 logs recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/notifications/archived` is nested. A dedicated `.notificationsArchived`
AppRoute case is added (pathSegment `notifications/archived` -> `.path` `/notifications/archived`
matching web exactly; Operations group alongside `.notifications` + `.notificationsAudit` +
`.notificationsWebhooks`; icon `archivebox.fill` — the SF Symbol parity of the web `Archive` glyph the
inbox uses for its "View archived" link). `AppRouteParser` aliases `/notifications/archived` ->
`.notificationsArchived` (required — the generic first-segment fallback would otherwise resolve
`.notifications`), plus an explicit `/notifications/inbox` -> `.notifications` alias documenting the web
`LegacyNotificationsRedirect` (/notifications -> /notifications/inbox). `ArchivedRouteRegistration`
hosts the page (with an `onNavigate` shell hook for the Back-to-inbox action), chained into
`\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift right after the Webhooks registration with
`onNavigate: { selection = $0 }`. So the page is reachable via the Operations-group sidebar entry and
any `/notifications/archived` deep link, and its Back-to-inbox control drives the shell selection to
the notifications inbox hub (`.notifications`). (Navigation registration is an allowed file per the
prompt.)

BACK-TO-INBOX TARGET RECONCILIATION: web links to `/notifications/inbox` (the InboxPage — a SEPARATE,
not-yet-shipped parity unit page:notifications/Inbox, OUT OF SCOPE here). Natively `/notifications` is
the inbox hub: web `LegacyNotificationsRedirect` forwards `/notifications` -> `/notifications/inbox`.
The Back-to-inbox affordance therefore targets `.notifications`. No InboxPage was created (covenant #2
— no scope creep into a sibling unit).

