================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI ArchivedPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable
ArchivedPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the three web i18n keys the page renders,
the copy-link share URL (web copyLink), the Back-to-inbox route target, and the embedded InboxBodyModel
built archived:true over an injectable InboxSource seam (production binds the shared KMP useNotificationLogs/
Groups + useAlertRules + useVehicles through the seam; the page re-surfaces vehicles/rules under the web
names). The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + copyLink + the Back-to-inbox
action) and hosts the already-shipped InboxBody feature view (its own P4 parity unit) fixed to the archived
tab — reused, not re-implemented (DRY) — so every web data state (loading / error / empty / content), the
day-grouped list, the per-row menu, the bulk-action set (Archive -> Restore), and the stale/offline chrome
render natively. A dedicated `.notificationsArchived` route (pathSegment `notifications/archived`,
Operations group) + parser alias + registration make it sidebar-reachable and `/notifications/archived`
deep-linkable, preserving every RouteTests invariant (verified by the harness). Verified on BOTH idioms by
isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency view type-checks (macOS 0/0 + iOS 0/0, incl. previews) and the executed
model + route harness (22/22 assertions passed). The full xcodebuild scheme was NOT run — it is gated on the
out-of-scope, P1-owned KMP `Shared.xcframework` Gradle staging that OOM-kills this shared host (per the
sibling logs), and triggering it would be irresponsible on a shared runner; deferred to its owner / the P99
integration gate.

